//@version=6
// ============================================================================
// Support & Resistance Zones [WavesUnchained]
// Version: 0.1.11
// Author: WavesUnchained
// Build: 2026-08-12 17:00:00
// ============================================================================
// Detector-driven support/resistance zone engine: independent zone detectors
// (pivot clusters, multiple tests, base/supply-demand, order blocks, fair
// value gaps, price gaps, equal-high/low liquidity) feed candidates into a
// central registry that merges, scores, confluences and tracks each zone
// through touch/reaction/break/flip lifecycle states. Detectors never draw
// directly — only the registry decides what becomes a zone and how it is
// rendered, which keeps detection, scoring and visualization independently
// testable and reusable for a future library extraction.
//
// Features:
//   ✓ Pivot cluster, multiple-test and base/supply-demand zone detectors
//   ✓ Order Block, Fair Value Gap, Price Gap and Equal High/Low Liquidity detectors
//   ✓ Central zone registry with ATR-based merging and stable zone IDs
//   ✓ Configurable confluence scoring (EMA, VWAP, Fibonacci, psychological levels, relative volume)
//   ✓ Zone lifecycle — touch detection, reaction validation, break detection, Support/Resistance flips
//   ✓ Nearest-zone renderer with hover tooltips (top N per side, score-filtered, non-overlapping)
//   ✓ On-chart zone state label (NEW/TESTED/CONFIRMED/WEAK/BROKEN/FLIPPED) — validity without hovering
//   ✓ Pine Log event logging and a validation statistics table for debugging
//
// Scores are heuristic confluence/quality scores, NOT statistical probabilities.
//
// ============================================================================

indicator(
     "Support & Resistance Zones [WavesUnchained]",
     shorttitle = "S/R Zones",
     overlay = true,
     max_bars_back = 5000,
     max_boxes_count = 250,
     max_labels_count = 350,
     max_lines_count = 100)

// ============================================================================
// 01 · GENERAL
// ============================================================================
